==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|run around like a chicken with no head}}
* {{l|en|run around like a headless chicken}}
* {{l|en|run around like a chicken with its head off}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[run around]] [[like a chicken with its head cut off]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To act in a [[haphazard]] or [[aimless]] way; to act [[frantically]] or without [[control]].
#: ''The liberal doesn't know what to do. She's running around '''like a chicken with its head cut off'''.''

